  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Release feed</h2>
    <p class="src-line">
      oh-my-niu keeps its own CHANGELOG. Latest 3 versions (changelogs.json, fetched 2026-10-19; the
      full feed lives on the <a href="/en/changelog/">changelog</a>):
    </p>
    <ul class="changelog-list">
      <li>
        <strong>2.0.0</strong>
        <span>
          Renamed oh-my-winuxsh → oh-my-niu (aligned with the niubash 1.0.0 branding); bundle/plugin
          API prefix <code>winuxsh:</code> → <code>niubash:</code>, env prefix now <code>NIU_*</code>;
          new first-party plugins command-timer / auto-env / dirmarks / git-fetch-reminder / env-sync;
          the git prompt segment resolves to the native Vcs segment for niubash 1.4.1+ (in-process
          rendering, zero git subprocesses).
        </span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>1.0.1</strong>
        <span>
          First source packs (Git/Docker/kubectl/npm/zoxide/direnv/dotenv/fzf/last-working-dir/thefuck);
          framework entry point, directory-first official plugins, prompt-core and the seven theme
          plugins minimal/classic/pure/compact/cyberpunk/forest/ocean; runtime smoke scripts;
          deterministic release packaging (zip + sha256).
        </span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>1.0.0</strong>
        <span>
          Founded as the official plugin bundle: bundle metadata (api = winuxsh:plugin-bundle@0.1.0,
          min_winuxsh 0.8.3), alias/completion/prompt-preset/keybinding/theme assets and author
          templates, deterministic release packaging with checksums.
        </span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Related links</h2>
    <div class="link-cols">
      <div>
